1
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:06,520
Hello.

2
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:11,560
This chapter, we'll learn about efficient and trendy figure drawing.

3
00:00:11,561 --> 00:00:15,640
For the first lesson, let's look at how to draw faces.

4
00:00:15,641 --> 00:00:18,440
Before we begin, let me give you a few notes.

5
00:00:18,441 --> 00:00:23,800
I won't be supplying materials like unnecessarily detailed anatomy references.

6
00:00:23,801 --> 00:00:25,560
Honestly, I don't know that much either.

7
00:00:25,561 --> 00:00:27,960
There's a lot of better material on the internet.

8
00:00:27,961 --> 00:00:33,080
In this class, we'll only go over the essential bones and muscles.

9
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:38,670
You don't have to copy-study the materials I provide.

10
00:00:38,671 --> 00:00:42,830
I just drew them to explain things, so you can understand them just by looking.

11
00:00:42,831 --> 00:00:44,830
Focus on grasping the shapes.

12
00:00:44,831 --> 00:00:45,831
And then practice.

13
00:00:46,670 --> 00:00:50,750
It's fine to copy-study, but don't copy-study mechanically and without meaning.

14
00:00:50,751 --> 00:00:54,270
I'll upload all the materials I've drawn.

15
00:00:54,271 --> 00:00:57,550
The face is the most important part of the human body.

16
00:00:57,630 --> 00:01:02,990
It's so important that I'd say the quality of the face accounts for more than half the quality of a drawing.

17
00:01:03,835 --> 00:01:08,470
Even if the design is mediocre, sometimes it won't catch the eye because of the face.

18
00:01:08,471 --> 00:01:11,430
And this applies to your pictures too.

19
00:01:11,430 --> 00:01:15,030
That's not to say you should obsess over only the face, though.

20
00:01:15,031 --> 00:01:19,590
It determines the first impression of a drawing, so I hope you'll treat it as important.

21
00:01:19,591 --> 00:01:22,720
When you practice faces, first grasp the shape of the skull.

22
00:01:23,324 --> 00:01:29,270
No matter how well you draw the eyes, nose, and mouth, if you can't place them to fit the skull's shape, the drawing feels clumsy.

23
00:01:29,270 --> 00:01:31,110
In bad cases, it can even give an unpleasant feeling.

24
00:01:32,009 --> 00:01:40,490
Just as a building is sturdy when its rebar structure is sturdy, there's a big difference between drawing a face while knowing the skull's shape and drawing one without knowing it.

25
00:01:40,491 --> 00:01:44,410
I mentioned earlier that shape is especially important in realism-style drawing.

26
00:01:44,411 --> 00:01:48,330
I recommend looking at photos of skulls online and copying them.

27
00:01:49,654 --> 00:01:51,760
I've drawn a skull here.

28
00:01:51,761 --> 00:01:54,400
And I've simplified it into angular shapes.

29
00:01:54,879 --> 00:01:57,200
The face isn't as flat as you'd think.

30
00:01:57,419 --> 00:02:02,480
The more you bring out these curved surfaces, the more realistic the face can look.

31
00:02:02,481 --> 00:02:04,720
We'll also examine the finer curves.

32
00:02:04,721 --> 00:02:11,680
Because the face is made of small muscles, even when muscle and flesh cover it, the skull's shape shows through on the outside.

33
00:02:11,681 --> 00:02:14,800
Especially, let's focus on the shape of the eye sockets and the cheekbones.

34
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:21,000
This part I've painted red is what I consider especially important when drawing a face.

35
00:02:21,001 --> 00:02:24,120
Once you've grasped the skull's shape, let's add flesh.

36
00:02:24,121 --> 00:02:29,320
Apply the same approach you use when studying the body, starting broad and gradually getting finer.

37
00:02:29,321 --> 00:02:33,480
Study the big shapes first, then the finer muscles.

38
00:02:33,481 --> 00:02:35,800
There's a large eyeball inside the eye socket.

39
00:02:35,801 --> 00:02:37,720
The eyeball is bigger than you'd think.

40
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,080
It's big enough to fill the eye socket.

41
00:02:40,019 --> 00:02:43,400
When you add the flesh, it looks like this.

42
00:02:43,401 --> 00:02:45,720
Compare it with the face sketch on the left.

43
00:02:46,295 --> 00:02:52,841
What matters here is that the curve of the eyeball also affects the curve of the final face surface.

44
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:56,600
I've always kept this in mind while drawing.

45
00:02:56,924 --> 00:03:00,321
It's good to observe by comparing with real photos of people.

46
00:03:04,055 --> 00:03:07,481
I've been drawing the structure around the eyes from various angles.

47
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:13,721
If you completely master this complex structure, you'll be able to draw more realistic faces.

48
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:18,060
I've drawn an incorrect example and a correct example.

49
00:03:19,445 --> 00:03:22,750
If you look closely at this red part, it isn't as dark as you'd think.

50
00:03:22,751 --> 00:03:24,190
Compare them.

51
00:03:24,191 --> 00:03:29,550
The part marked in green should be the darkest in most lighting situations.

52
00:03:31,055 --> 00:03:35,560
Try to understand the curve and angle of the surface around the eyes and apply them to your drawing.

53
00:03:41,079 --> 00:03:49,290
The nose and mouth are made up of many muscles and cartilage joining together into a complex structure, making them one of the hardest parts for beginners to draw.

54
00:03:49,291 --> 00:03:52,371
Study this drawing where the shape is emphasized.

55
00:03:53,715 --> 00:03:58,620
It's good to think of the nose as three masses when drawing it.

56
00:03:58,621 --> 00:04:01,500
It's also nice to express the curve beside the nose.

57
00:04:01,501 --> 00:04:06,821
If you overdo it, it becomes nasolabial folds, but if you express it well, it also makes the drawing look realistic.

58
00:04:07,424 --> 00:04:09,740
It's the same with the philtrum.

59
00:04:09,741 --> 00:04:14,460
There's actually a procedure called a noble lift that raises the philtrum and the bridge of the nose.

60
00:04:14,461 --> 00:04:18,661
If you draw this area as if it's slightly raised, the image looks more refined.

61
00:04:20,350 --> 00:04:25,080
The upper lip can be divided into two main masses.

62
00:04:25,530 --> 00:04:28,220
It's important to draw the center of the lips well.

63
00:04:28,860 --> 00:04:31,340
The lips aren't flat.

64
00:04:31,341 --> 00:04:39,420
This red line is what I emphasize when drawing a woman's lips, and it makes the lips look slightly curled up, as if inverted.

65
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:45,150
The lower lip can be divided into three main parts.

66
00:04:45,151 --> 00:04:50,270
Think of it as a flat, a curve, and a flat structure.

67
00:04:50,271 --> 00:04:52,030
Flat, curve, flat.

68
00:04:53,555 --> 00:04:58,780
When people draw women, they tend not to show the curves around the mouth.

69
00:04:58,781 --> 00:05:01,020
They say it's because it makes them look thin.

70
00:05:01,021 --> 00:05:04,700
But I always make sure to express this part too.

71
00:05:04,701 --> 00:05:07,100
It makes it a bit more realistic.

72
00:05:07,101 --> 00:05:08,700
Let's check by looking at my drawings.

73
00:05:11,125 --> 00:05:13,550
I've marked them with red lines.

74
00:05:15,395 --> 00:05:19,031
It's faint, but it's definitely expressed.

75
00:05:24,350 --> 00:05:31,040
In profile, it's good when the lips don't fully close when you draw a straight line from the nose to the chin.

76
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:40,551
When drawing ears, you also establish the big flow first, then render.

77
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:46,110
You should draw them like a concave dish shape.

78
00:05:46,111 --> 00:05:47,550
Draw them a lot.

79
00:05:47,551 --> 00:05:52,990
For the position behind, find the center of the side-view head and place it a bit behind.

80
00:05:54,965 --> 00:06:04,110
When drawing a realistic face, you have to be unhesitating about showing the hollow beside the nose, like the nasolabial folds, the shading on the cheekbones, and the philtrum.

81
00:06:04,111 --> 00:06:10,190
You've probably seen photos where these areas are smoothed out during retouching, and they look awkward and obviously edited.

82
00:06:10,191 --> 00:06:13,630
That's far from my drawing style, which pursues naturalness.

83
00:06:13,631 --> 00:06:16,910
If expression is difficult for you, it's also good to draw an elderly person.

84
00:06:16,911 --> 00:06:20,391
You can express these things relatively easily and without hesitation.

85
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:26,880
I have to bring up proportions.

86
00:06:26,881 --> 00:06:31,760
I don't draw by calculating proportions mathematically, but I've analyzed my own drawings in my own way.

87
00:06:31,761 --> 00:06:32,960
Let's take the front view as the baseline.

88
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:44,261
The forehead line, the starting point of the eyebrows, the center base of the nose, and the chin line have a ratio of one to one to one.

89
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:52,440
The horizontal length of the eye and the distance between the eyes have a one to one to one ratio too.

90
00:06:55,850 --> 00:07:04,090
When you draw a triangle connecting the center of the eyes and the center of the lips, the tip of the nose touches the two ends of the nose.

91
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:13,960
For women, this triangle is close to equilateral, and for men it's a longer triangle top to bottom.

92
00:07:13,961 --> 00:07:19,000
That's because when I draw women, I prefer to draw the midface a bit shorter.

93
00:07:19,001 --> 00:07:21,560
It gets even shorter with a younger age.

94
00:07:21,561 --> 00:07:32,280
I draw it shorter for East Asians than Westerners, because the juvenile features that keep a child's face into adulthood are especially prominent in East Asians.

95
00:07:32,281 --> 00:07:35,320
In Korea especially, a short midface is preferred.

96
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:36,520
That's right.

97
00:07:36,521 --> 00:07:45,880
Compared to East Asians, Westerners have deeper-set eyes, a higher nose, and a longer head shape front to back.

98
00:07:45,881 --> 00:07:56,040
Most East Asians have a shorter head shape, which is relatively flatter, with shallower eyelids, and a wider gap between the eyebrows, compared to Westerners.

99
00:07:57,265 --> 00:08:03,011
You might think a short head shape is a drawback of East Asians from an aesthetic standpoint, but it's not at all.

100
00:08:03,505 --> 00:08:06,931
There are plenty of handsome and beautiful celebrities with short head shapes.

101
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:11,210
Let's gather photos of beautiful people from both East and West, compare them, and study.

102
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:20,650
Now that we've learned about shape, let's look at the process of simplifying a drawing.

103
00:08:20,651 --> 00:08:24,810
From left to right, it shows the drawing getting more and more simplified.

104
00:08:25,450 --> 00:08:31,530
The picture on the far right only has the relatively important parts I've been explaining so far.

105
00:08:31,531 --> 00:08:34,570
You can quickly show just the overall shape.

106
00:08:34,571 --> 00:08:38,409
The shapes of the eyes, nose, and mouth get established as you color.

107
00:08:38,410 --> 00:08:41,130
You could call it a sketch specialized for coloring.

108
00:08:41,535 --> 00:08:43,929
Let me show you through an example.

109
00:09:09,230 --> 00:09:12,160
You sketch while thinking about the skull's structure.

110
00:09:12,161 --> 00:09:14,880
You determine the positions of the eye sockets, mouth, and ears.

111
00:09:15,765 --> 00:09:18,560
The lines don't need to be clean.

112
00:09:18,561 --> 00:09:21,040
You draw while keeping the face proportions in mind.

113
00:09:25,530 --> 00:09:26,780
You lay down the base color.

114
00:09:26,781 --> 00:09:30,220
You can start dark or start light.

115
00:09:30,221 --> 00:09:31,580
There's no set rule.

116
00:09:31,581 --> 00:09:36,300
What matters is that you build it up broadly with simple surfaces of about two tones.

117
00:09:36,301 --> 00:09:38,940
It resembles the process of sculpting.

118
00:09:38,941 --> 00:09:41,861
You draw with the idea of adding flesh a bit at a time.

119
00:09:42,310 --> 00:09:45,541
You gradually make the brush smaller to do finer rendering.

120
00:09:50,725 --> 00:09:53,040
Then you add line drawing on top.

121
00:09:54,325 --> 00:09:58,800
This way, you can get through the early stages quickly.

122
00:09:58,801 --> 00:10:03,360
Light, color, and detailed coloring will be covered in later chapters.

123
00:10:03,361 --> 00:10:06,080
Let's focus on the big masses.

124
00:10:06,081 --> 00:10:08,240
Let's work on faces in a variety of compositions.

125
00:27:41,179 --> 00:27:45,950
This time, we learned about facial anatomy and the simplified drawing process.

126
00:27:45,950 --> 00:27:49,790
Next time, we'll learn about the anatomy of the torso and the simplified drawing process.

127
00:27:50,190 --> 00:27:51,190
Great work.
